        "reference": "Helaman 16:15",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Some things they may have guessed right, among so many; but behold, we know that all these great and marvelous works cannot come to pass, of which has been spoken.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 16:16",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And they began to reason and to contend among themselves, saying:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 16:17",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "That it is not reasonable that such a being as a Christ shall come; if so, and he be the Son of God, the Father of heaven and of earth, as it has been spoken, why will he not show himself unto us as well as unto them who shall be at Jerusalem?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Alma 30:53."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 30:53.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 30:53",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 30,
                    "end": 30,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 53,
                        "end": 53
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 16:18",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, why will he not show himself in this land as well as in the land of Jerusalem?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 16:19",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, we know that this is a wicked tradition, which has been handed down unto us by our fathers, to cause us that we should believe in some great and marvelous thing which should come to pass, but not among us, but in a land which is far distant, a land which we know not; therefore they can keep us in ignorance, for we cannot witness with our own eyes that they are true.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Traditions of Men."
          },
          {
            "start": 335,
            "end": 342,
            "text": "Alma 30:15; Ether 12:5 (5–6, 19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Traditions of Men.",
            "prettyString": "TG Traditions of Men",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
